      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "PTCA is a new technique for the treatment of certain patients with coronary artery disease. It involves dilatation of stenotic segments of artery using a balloon catheter, and is carried out in cardiac catheterization laboratories. If successful, the need for coronary bypass surgery may be removed, although some patients with initially successful PTCA will come to surgery eventually. Successful PTCA is associated with relief of angina, improved angiographic appearances and coronary perfusion. The primary success rate is between 65% and 80%, and the restenosis rate approximately 25%. 80% of patients will be angina free one year after PTCA. In this paper the indications, contraindications, technology, results and complications are discussed."},
